  message: "P4 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 9ae4abe13f; owner-requested re-check of open P4 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p4_review_11012026/langs1/). VERDICT: CURRENT. Reviewed 2026-11-01 on dev 9ae4abe13f (fx_naviz: class A: class B: def go). Survey emits method 'B.go' with qualified_name 'B.go' and class B with qualified_name 'B'. The py.py:3542-3543 comment still calls the scope qualification separate work. A.B().go() calls from A.run and top resolve only to external_symbol go/B, so the call-resolution effect this item says to measure first is live. Premise holds. Changing name/qualified_name to the full chain would trigger WI-fazid's latent split('.')[0] bug. MECHANISM: python qualified_name is set to the emitted name (innermost class + member), not the full __qualname__ scope chain. SHARES MECHANISM WITH: WI-fazid."  # 1e0c
